xpad version 0.2.1 README
-----------------------

xpad is a virtual sticky pad system for X using GTK+.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION NOTES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     To compile, just type "make" and / or "make install".

     Read the INSTALL file for more.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE NOTES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Right click to obtain configuration options and open new pads.
		You can also run xpad again to open a new pad.

	Closing a pad saves the contents for later.  Destroying one destroys
		the contents.

     Hold down CTRL and left drag to move a pad.  Hold down CTRL and right
          drag to resize a pad.
     
     Add xpad to your ~/.xinitrc to have xpad start with every X boot.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND ARGUMENTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Standard GTK+ arguments are understood.  In addition, the following
		arguments are available.

	--version:		Prints version information.

	--sync-time=%d:	Where %d is the number of seconds between each 
					"sync," or saving of the pad's contents.  Entering
					0 indicates no syncing.  Default is 60.


